ghty-four lakh species and attains a body. In the Bhagavad Gita, these cunning people are called dhushkino mudhah. Those who are not Krishna conscious,\nsuch non-devotees have to engage in sinful deeds. Therefore, they are foolish, meaning they are stupid and cunning. They are such fools\nthat they do not even know what will happen to them in the next life. Although they see all kinds of\nanimals eating disgusting things—such as pigs eating excrement, crocodiles eating all kinds of\nfish, etc., etc., due to eating such useless things, in the next life they will be forced to eat extremely despicable\nthings. A Vaishnava is always afraid of such a wicked life and such a"
