ना चाहिए कि कृष्ण के बिना कोई सुखी नहीं हो\nसकता। इस तरह कृष्णभावनाभावित व्यक्ति सभी प्रकार के छद्म-आध्यात्मवादियों, चिन्तकों,\nएकेश्वरवादियों, दार्शनिकों तथा परोपकारियों से दूर रहता है।",
      "textEn": "391\n\nFor a devotee, living in heaven or hell is the same, because the devotee neither lives in heaven nor hell,\nbut he lives with Krishna in the spiritual world. The essence of a devotee's success is not known to workers and\nknowledgeable people. Therefore, the workers want to be happy through material manipulation, and\nthe wise want to be happy by becoming one with God. But such is not the interest of a devotee. He is not interested in going to the Himalayas or the jungle and doing so-called meditation. Instead, he shows interest in the most busy part of the world, where he teaches people about Krishna consciousness. The Krishna Bhavanamrut movement was launched with this objective. We do not teach anyone to meditate in a secluded place\nso that they can show that they have progressed and they can feel proud of their\nso-called divine meditation, even if they are busy in all kinds of foolish\nphysical activities.\nPrahlad Maharaj, like a Vaishnav, is never in favor of deceiving in spiritual progress. In contrast, he is interested in awakening Krishna consciousness in people,\nbecause this is the only means by which they can become happy. Prahlada Maharaj clearly says—Nanyam\nTvasya Sharanam Bhramatu Anupashye—I know that without the nectar of Krishna consciousness, that is, without taking refuge in your lotus feet, no one can be happy. A human being keeps wandering in this universe for lifetimes,\nbut by the grace of a devotee, Shri Chaitanya Mahaprabhu's servant, he can come to know about Krishna Bhava Namrata,\nand then he can not only become happy in this world but can also return to the abode of God. That is the ultimate goal of life. Members of the Krishna Bhava Namrata movement do not have interest in going to the Himalayas or the forest, where man can only demonstrate meditation. Nor are they\ninterested in opening many schools of yoga and meditation in cities. The opposite is the Krishna consciousness movement.\nThis is the goal.\nEach member goes door to door and is interested in trying to convince people about the teachings of the Bhagavad Gita or about the teachings of God\nChaitanya. The Hare Krishna movement's\nThis is the goal. That the members should have complete faith that no one can be happy without Krishna.\nCannot. In this way, a person imbued with Krishna consciousness stays away from all kinds of pseudo-spiritualists, thinkers,\nmonotheists, philosophers, and philanthropists."
